# Wave W17-U (Route 201): candor elm — a young shore elm in light, yellow-leaning greens, broad-crowned over the first meadow with the highlight lifted clear of the turf, on candor turf (ground baked in). Route 201’s own tree — younger and lighter than Route 202’s mature approach oak beside it, and split from Route 117’s field elm (Maris) by crown register: the shore elm leans to the lake light, the field elm shades worked land.
